Error [E1102]: `greet` can't be sent because `fn()` isn't sendable
  --> tests/ui/unsendable_send.jet:7:17
    |
  7 |     sender.send(greet)
    |                 ^^^^^
 Why: a closure may hold outside state, so it must be handed over with `take` before it crosses this boundary; tasks and channels move owned values between threads
 Fix: send plain owned data instead, or rebuild the value as an owned copy before calling `.send()`
